// The look: how the scene's light becomes the picture. The renderer draws
// into a half-float frame (render's Post), lit by render's one lighting
// convention: the sun's colour an irradiance, the ambient light and the sky
// a radiance, a glow a radiance, all of it multiplied by the exposure as it
// is drawn. The Post then blooms the frame and tone-maps it into the
// window's texture.
//
// For now the picture is the one drawn straight into the window before:
// no tone mapping (the frame clamped), no bloom, an exposure of 1.

// The Post's settings
pub fn lookPost(post &mut Post) {
  post.toneMapper = TONE_MAP_NONE;
  post.bloom = 0.;
  post.exposure = 1.;
}

// The renderer's exposure under 'sky'
pub fn exposureFor(sky &SkyLook) f32 { 1.; }
